WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:08.000
The outside wheel follows a longer path.

00:08.000 --> 00:12.000
The difference: why cannot both driven wheels stay locked together?

00:12.000 --> 00:18.000
Lock both wheels to one speed, and the inside tire must scrub.

00:18.000 --> 00:22.000
The drive pinion turns the crown gear and carrier.

00:22.000 --> 00:28.000
Inside, planet pinions let the two axle shafts turn at different speeds.

00:29.000 --> 00:34.000
Suppose the inside wheel turns at 27 rpm and the outside at 33.

00:34.000 --> 00:38.000
Carrier speed is their average: 30 rpm.

00:38.000 --> 00:43.000
Each wheel follows its path; neither has to drag.

00:43.000 --> 00:48.000
Differential: two wheels, each with its own speed.
